   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The model is \\( \\frac{dU}{dt} = kU \\). Separating and integrating gives \\( \\ln|U| = kt + C \\), so \\( U = U_0 e^{kt} \\), and the value at t = 0 gives \\( U_0 = 560 \\).",
         "rule_named": "separation of variables for proportional growth"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The second value gives \\( 2240 = 560 e^{4k} \\), so \\( k = \\frac{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{4} \\).",
         "rule_named": "constant from a second data pair"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Therefore \\( U(t) = 560 e^{\\frac{t \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{4}} \\) users.",
